    {
      "id": "node_b3fdad12-aa8a-4d1f-a50c-bc43654bb903",
      "name": "socket_accept",
      "kind": "Processor",
      "parentId": "root",
      "children": [],
      "incomingLinks": [
        "992f1269-5aa2-4929-91a3-5745c23f6cb9",
        "link_47dfe6fa-791b-4863-99ff-002db0ff8f88",
        "link_559f3fef-7b5a-4d0e-9d55-8f70aa5c46b8",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "outgoingLinks": [
        "link_66e6e8e4-5fb1-4171-8bc9-1d22a4323ec5",
        "link_ff70c67f-8f63-48a5-9b9a-df23d3686dfd"
      ],
      "layout": {
        "x": 721.8808300298551,
        "y": 1168.411607170984,
        "width": 200.0,
        "height": 138.0,
        "closedWidth": 200.0,
        "closedHeight": 138.0,
        "openWidth": 200.0,
        "openHeight": 138.0,
        "isExpanded": true
      },
      "fileLayoutStrategyId": "single-file",
      "text": {
        "source": "enum { HELD_CAPACITY = 256 };\nstatic ReqRep held[HELD_CAPACITY]; /* resolved responses waiting for their pending request */\nstatic size_t held_count = 0U;\nstatic unsigned long sequence = 0UL;\nstatic unsigned long resolved_total = 0UL;\nstatic long limit = -1;\nint running = 1;\nReqRep item;\n\nif (limit < 0) {\n    const char *text = getenv(\"WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS\");\n    limit = text != NULL ? atol(text) : 0;\n}\n/* 1. Hold every resolved response until its pending request comes round. */\nwhile (threadwork_buffer_count(response) > 0U) {\n    if (pop(response, &item) != THREADWORK_OK) {\n        return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n    }\n    if (held_count == HELD_CAPACITY) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"webserver: more than %d unmatched responses\\n\", HELD_CAPACITY);\n        return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n    }\n    held[held_count++] = item;\n}\n/* 2. Resolve matching pending requests; recirculate the others. */\nwhile (threadwork_buffer_count(awaitResponseLoop_in) > 0U) {\n    size_t index = 0U;\n\n    if (pop(awaitResponseLoop_in, &item) != THREADWORK_OK) {\n        return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n    }\n    while (index < held_count && strcmp(held[index].id, item.id) != 0) {\n        index++;\n    }\n    if (index == held_count) {\n        if (push(awaitResponseLoop_out, &item) != THREADWORK_OK) {\n            return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n        }\n        continue;\n    }\n    if (libhttp->http_resolve(&item, &held[index]) != 0) {\n        fprintf(stderr, \"webserver: client closed the connection early\\n\");\n    }\n    held[index] = held[--held_count];\n    resolved_total++;\n    if (limit > 0 && resolved_total >= (unsigned long)limit) {\n        (void)threadwork_runner__shutdown_request(&threadwork_runner);\n    }\n}\n/* 3. Accept at most one connection; wait briefly only when nothing is in flight. */\n(void)threadwork_runner__is_running(&threadwork_runner, &running);\nif (running) {\n    int idle = held_count == 0U && threadwork_buffer_count(awaitResponseLoop_out) == 0U;\n\n    if (libhttp->http_wait(idle ? 25 : 0)) {\n        int accepted = libhttp->http_accept(++sequence, &item);\n\n        if (accepted < 0) {\n            return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n        }\n        if (accepted > 0\n            && (push(request, &item) != THREADWORK_OK\n                || push(awaitResponseLoop_out, &item) != THREADWORK_OK)) {\n            return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n        }\n    }\n} else if (held_count == 0U && threadwork_buffer_count(awaitResponseLoop_out) == 0U) {\n    libhttp->http_close();\n}",
        "sourceLanguageId": "",
        "initialization": "const char *port_text = getenv(\"WEBSERVER_PORT\");\nconst char *any_text = getenv(\"WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY\");\nint port = port_text != NULL ? atoi(port_text) : 8080;\nint any_address = any_text != NULL && strcmp(any_text, \"1\") == 0;\n\nif (libhttp->http_listen(port, any_address) != 0) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"webserver: cannot listen on port %d\\n\", port);\n    return THREADWORK_ERROR;\n}\nprintf(\"webserver: listening on http://%s:%d\\n\", any_address ? \"0.0.0.0\" : \"127.0.0.1\", port);\n(void)fflush(stdout);",
        "initializationLanguageId": "",
        "specification": "Entry and exit point of every request.\n\nInitialization: read WEBSERVER_PORT and WEBSERVER_BIND_ANY, open the listener with\nlibhttp.http_listen and print \"webserver: listening on http://<address>:<port>\".\nFailure to listen is an error (the process exits non-zero).\n\nEach tick:\n1. Pop every resolved ReqRep from `response` and hold it (≤ 256) until its pending request\n   is seen.\n2. Pop every pending ReqRep from awaitResponseLoop_in. If a held response has the same id,\n   resolve it with libhttp.http_resolve (write the reply, log it, close, free), otherwise push\n   it back on awaitResponseLoop_out.\n3. While running, accept at most one connection with libhttp.http_accept and push the new\n   ReqRep to both `request` (router) and awaitResponseLoop_out (pending copy). Wait up to\n   25 ms for a connection only when nothing is held or pending.\n4. Count resolutions; at WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS request shutdown.\nAfter shutdown, stop accepting and close the listener once nothing is held or pending.",
        "specificationLanguageId": "markdown",
        "tests": "- With an unused port, startup prints the listening URL and the process keeps running.\n- With the port already in use, initialization fails and the process exits non-zero.\n- Two concurrent clients receive the responses matching their own requests (ids differ).\n- WEBSERVER_MAX_REQUESTS=1 exits 0 after exactly one access-log line.",
        "testsLanguageId": "json",
        "aiInstructions": "",
        "aiInstructionsLanguageId": "markdown"
      },
